  <prompt>Run the quality-assessment Workflow READ-ONLY across the shared server libraries — src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core, Spaarke.Dataverse, Spaarke.Scheduling (~10k LOC). Produce a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design.md and append this surface's SCORECARD row. This surface roots the two-Dataverse-stacks question (NG1) — and per the 2026-08-13 decision, NG1 is now on an ASSESS-THEN-DECIDE track owned by THIS task: the design.md MUST include the verified NG1 access-stack unification design (ServiceClient vs raw-HTTP, ~22 files) with a fresh re-estimate and a proceed/defer recommendation. NG1 scope now includes the #3(b) shared-lib ClientSecret→MI credential migration (entangled with the access stacks); task 060 lands only the vestigial separate-app-reg drop (#3a). Modify NO source.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer running the standing quality-assessment method. This surface underpins the BFF + plugins; the ServiceClient-vs-raw-HTTP stack split originates here. Follow ADRs strictly; the assessment is read-only.</role>
    <goal>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/shared-server-libs/design.md exists — a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design for the shared server libs that ALSO carries the verified NG1 section: the two-Dataverse-access-stacks unification design (ServiceClient vs raw-HTTP), a fresh file/effort/risk re-estimate superseding the stale "~25-30 files, 4-6 weeks" figure, and an explicit proceed/defer recommendation for the remaining remediation (decided on facts; the #3(b) shared-lib credential migration is included in NG1 scope; task 060 = the #3a app-reg drop only) — and notes/SCORECARD.md carries this surface's verified D1–D11 row.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-05 + design.md §7 (surface #2, roots the Dataverse-stack question). The BFF pass already confirmed DataverseServiceClientImpl vs raw-HTTP stack + always-failing casts. NG1 STATUS CHANGE (2026-08-13, project CLAUDE.md decision): NG1 is no longer "deferred out of scope" — it is on an assess-then-decide track and THIS task owns producing the verified NG1 design + re-estimate. **NG1 scope now INCLUDES the shared-lib credential migration #3(b)**: task 060 (#3a) only drops the *vestigial separate* Dataverse S2S app-reg (scripts/docs/KV, zero code consumers). The BFF's OWN shared-lib Dataverse path is STILL secret-based (DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:40-64 `AuthType=ClientSecret`; DataverseWebApiService.cs:40-56 hard-requires `Dataverse:ClientSecret`; DataverseOptions.cs:32 `[Required]`+ValidateOnStart — full grounding in notes/deployment-refactors-assessment-2026-08-12.md §Addendum 2026-08-13). Migrating it to MI is an IDENTITY-ATTRIBUTION change entangled with the two access-stack files, so #3(b) is decided AS PART of this NG1 design — the credential migration and the access-stack unification are reasoned about together (same files, same identity question). It's a live ADR-028:24 MUST (no amendment), flagged report-only by task 040 rule (c) until this design lands it. This assessment re-estimates NG1 (access-stack unification + the #3(b) credential migration) with a fresh file/effort/risk census superseding the stale "~25-30 files, 4-6 weeks" figure, and DECIDES remediation on facts: a proceed recommendation (with tranches) or a documented defer with specific blocking evidence. Remediation EXECUTION happens via separately created tasks after this design exists — this task remains read-only.</background>
    <relevant-files>
