  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: READ-ONLY (NFR-03) — no src/ modification; only outputs are the surface design.md + SCORECARD row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: the Fable adversarial-verification pass is non-negotiable (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (NG1 — UPDATED 2026-08-13, supersedes the "characterize only" rule): the design MUST include a verified NG1 section — the two-Dataverse-access-stacks unification design PLUS the #3(b) shared-lib ClientSecret→MI credential migration (they are entangled — same files, identity-attribution question — reason about them together), with a fresh re-estimate and an explicit proceed/defer recommendation — but MUST NOT execute any unification or migration (read-only task; remediation tasks are created from the design). Task 060 is ONLY the vestigial-app-reg drop (#3a); do NOT assume it migrated the credential code. The BFF workstream still only collapses the app-only downcast boilerplate (task 021 — a cast pattern, not the credential source). Update the NG1 Idea (#742) reference in the design to reflect the assess-then-decide status.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-gate">The NG1 #3b credential-migration analysis MUST consume the BFF Auth Surface Map (task 019 → notes/bff-auth-surface-map.md) — its secret/identity→consumer dependency graph + identity model (system-vs-UAMI) + OBO-shared-secret findings are the verified input for deciding the shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration and its identity-attribution impact. Do not re-derive the auth picture; build on the map.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-map-2026-08-13">#3b design MUST account for the map's findings: (1) `DataverseWebApiClient.cs:42` prefers the secret when present over MI — a code change, not just config; (2) config-key removal ≠ KV-secret removal (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` = one KV secret under 5 config keys / 9 consumers — never-remove; only its Dataverse-app-only consumers migrate); (3) the Dataverse Application User must be registered for the **UAMI** SP (not the stale `56ae2188…` in template:79); (4) `prvActOnBehalfOfAnotherUser` re-grant is needed for the MI identity; (5) `DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:49-77` is the one file mixing app-only + OBO CCA — split surgically, preserve OBO.</constraint>
  </constraints>

