  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/shared-server-libs/design.md exists, Fable-verified, with severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, the NG1 section exists with (a) a verified access-stack unification design, (b) a fresh file/effort/risk re-estimate against the post-task-060 baseline (superseding "~25-30 files, 4-6 weeks"), and (c) an explicit proceed/defer recommendation with evidence — and NO unification was executed by this task (design decides; separately created tasks execute).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, the #3(b) shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration is included in the NG1 design's scope (entangled with the access stacks), and task 060 (#3a) is treated as the vestigial-app-reg drop only — not the code migration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, notes/SCORECARD.md has this surface's verified row appended; no aggregate published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/ was modified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-05. NG1 REFRAMED 2026-08-13 (project CLAUDE.md decision): assess-then-decide, owned here — this design + re-estimate DECIDES the remaining access-stack remediation on facts; no longer "deferred out of scope". Task 060 = #3a (vestigial separate-app-reg drop) only; the #3(b) shared-lib ClientSecret→MI migration is part of THIS NG1 design (grounding: assessment §Addendum 2026-08-13). Update the NG1 Idea (#742) with this task's verdict. Remediation tasks still deferred until this design exists.</notes>

